  "summary": "Recent preprints and a published algorithm extend species tree, network consensus, and rooted tree partitioning methods.",
  "synthesis": "Across these items, the common thread is algorithmic reformulation of core phylogenetic tree tasks, from consensus and species tree inference to partitioning of rooted trees. The level-1 network consensus method (L1N, implemented in PhyloSummaries) is reported to outperform prior methods on simulated data. QUANTA recasts weighted quartet bipartitioning as a QUBO problem for quantum annealing on D-Wave hardware for species tree estimation. QRAFT pursues scalability within a statistically consistent coalescent framework, inferring million-taxon trees with near-linear time and linear memory. PhytClust, a published work, gives an exact and threshold-free optimization of monophyletic partitioning for rooted trees. The dominant theme is new computational formulations and tractability for tree-level problems; the items differ in methodology.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-07"
